<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/bolus-insulin-only-for-bolus-feeding> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Bolus insulin only for bolus feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "bolus-insulin-only-for-bolus-feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Bolus insulin only is of particular use for bolus feeding. For bolus feeds given over 4-6 hours, a single dose of soluble human insulin, administered 20 minutes prior to the start of the bolus feed can be given. For bolus feeds given as a bolus or over < 4 hours an analogue insulin, administered 0-15 minutes prior to administration of the feed can be given to cover the carbohydrate content." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "•  Bolus insulin only is of particular use for bolus feeding. For bolus feeds given over 4-6 hours, a single dose of soluble human insulin, administered 20 minutes prior to the start of the bolus feed can be given. For bolus feeds given as a bolus or over < 4 hours an analogue insulin, administered 0-15 minutes prior to administration of the feed can be given to cover the carbohydrate content." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/bolus-insulin-only-for-multiple-short-feeds> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Bolus insulin only for multiple short feeds" ;
    dmo:populationScope "people with Type 1 or insulin deficient diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "bolus-insulin-only-for-multiple-short-feeds" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "For bolus feeds given over 4-6 hours, a single doses of soluble human insulin, administered 20 minutes prior to the start of the bolus feed can be given. For bolus feeds given as a bolus or over < 4 hours an analogue insulin, administered 0-15 minutes prior to administration of the feed can be given to cover the carbohydrate content. This would not be used for any patient with basal insulin requirements." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For bolus feeds given over 4-6 hours, a single doses of soluble human insulin, administered 20 minutes prior to the start of the bolus feed can be given. For bolus feeds given as a bolus or over < 4 hours an analogue insulin, administered 0-15 minutes prior to administration of the feed can be given to cover the carbohydrate content. This would not be used for any patient with basal insulin requirements." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/bolus-regimen-examples> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Bolus regimen examples" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with non Type 1/insulin deficient diabetes receiving enteral feeding using VRIII" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "bolus-regimen-examples" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Analogue = Novorapid 8 units at start of feed and then 4, 8, 12 and 16 hours into feed" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Analogue = Novorapid 8 units at start of feed and then 4, 8, 12 and 16 hours into feed" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Soluble = Actrapid 13 units at start of feed and then 6 and 12 hours into feed" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/calculate-total-feed-dose-tfd-by-subtracting-20-from-total-insulin-used-on-vriii-during-feed> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Calculate total feed dose (TFD) by subtracting 20% from total insulin used on VRIII during feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "calculate-total-feed-dose-tfd-by-subtracting-20-from-total-insulin-used-on-vriii-during-feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Add up the total insulin dose used on the VRIII for the duration of the feed and take off 20%. This provides the total insulin requirement for during feed, known as the total feed dose (TFD)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Add up the total insulin dose used on the VRIII for the duration of the feed and take off 20%. This provides the total insulin requirement for during feed, known as the total feed dose (TFD)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

