<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/total-feed-related-insulin-dose> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Total feed related insulin dose" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with non Type 1/insulin deficient diabetes receiving enteral feeding using VRIII" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "total-feed-related-insulin-dose" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Total feed related insulin dose = 50 units - 20% = 40 units" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Step 2 - Total feed related insulin dose = 50 units - 20% = 40 units" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/transition-from-mixed-insulin-to-basal-insulin-in-hospitalized-patients> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Transition from mixed insulin to basal insulin in hospitalized patients" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with any type of diabetes admitted to hospital on a mixed insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "transition-from-mixed-insulin-to-basal-insulin-in-hospitalized-patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Conditional" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "People with any type of diabetes, admitted to hospital on a mixed insulin should be reviewed by the DIT at the earliest opportunity. These patients should be commenced on basal insulin to mimic their usual basal insulin doses received from their usual mixed insulin regimen minus 20%. For example, if a patient is on 20 units of Humulin M3 (or Novomix 30) they receive 30% bolus insulin and 70% basal insulin, therefore they would require 11 units (14 units basal insulin - 20% = 11 units)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People with any type of diabetes, admitted to hospital on a mixed insulin should be reviewed by the DIT at the earliest opportunity. These patients should be commenced on basal insulin to mimic their usual basal insulin doses received from their usual mixed insulin regimen minus 20%. For example, if a patient is on 20 units of Humulin M3 (or Novomix 30) they receive 30% bolus insulin and 70% basal insulin, therefore they would require 11 units (14 units basal insulin - 20% = 11 units)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/treat-glucose-levels-4-0-mmol-l-immediately> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Treat glucose levels <4.0 mmol/L immediately" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes receiving enteral feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "treat-glucose-levels-4-0-mmol-l-immediately" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If glucose levels are <4.0 mmol/L treat immediately as per local guidance or JBDS-IP hypoglycaemia guidelines" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If glucose levels are <4.0 mmol/L treat immediately as per local guidance or JBDS-IP hypoglycaemia guidelines" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/treat-hypoglycaemia-promptly-if-blood-glucose-4-mmol-l-and-patient-has-no-iv-access> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Treat hypoglycaemia promptly if blood glucose <4 mmol/L and patient has no IV access" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with impaired swallow and with an enteral feeding tube in situ" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "treat-hypoglycaemia-promptly-if-blood-glucose-4-mmol-l-and-patient-has-no-iv-access" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If patient has no IV access give ONE of the following via enteral feeding tube: a. 2 tubes 40% glucose gel - not for use with fine bore enteral feeding tube b. 1 bottle (60ml) Lift® c. 150-200 ml orange juice d. 50-70ml Fortijuce® or equivalent (NOT Fortisip) to give 15-20g carbohydrate" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If patient has no IV access give ONE of the following via enteral feeding tube: a. 2 tubes 40% glucose gel - not for use with fine bore enteral feeding tube b. 1 bottle (60ml) Lift® c. 150-200 ml orange juice d. 50-70ml Fortijuce® or equivalent (NOT Fortisip) to give 15-20g carbohydrate" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/treat-type-3c-secondary-diabetes-as-type-1-if-insulin-deficient> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Treat Type 3c/Secondary diabetes as Type 1 if insulin deficient" ;
