<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-ivi-glucose-to-prevent-hypoglycaemia-when-feed-is-unexpectedly-stopped-with-feed-specific-basal-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of IVI glucose to prevent hypoglycaemia when feed is unexpectedly stopped with feed specific basal insulin" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients using feed specific basal insulin when feed is unexpectedly held or stopped" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-ivi-glucose-to-prevent-hypoglycaemia-when-feed-is-unexpectedly-stopped-with-feed-specific-basal-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Safety" ;
    dmo:statement "If a feed specific basal insulin is used and the feed is unexpectedly held or stopped, IVI glucose may be needed to prevent hypoglycaemia for the duration of the insulin action or until the feed is restarted" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If a feed specific basal insulin is used and the feed is unexpectedly held or stopped, IVI glucose may be needed to prevent hypoglycaemia for the duration of the insulin action or until the feed is restarted" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-lift-or-equivalent-for-acute-management-of-hypoglycaemia-in-patients-nil-by-mouth> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of Lift or equivalent for acute management of hypoglycaemia in patients nil by mouth" ;
    dmo:populationScope "patients nil by mouth" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-lift-or-equivalent-for-acute-management-of-hypoglycaemia-in-patients-nil-by-mouth" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "The preferred option of this writing group is the use of Lift (or equivalent) as this will deliver the required rapid acting carbohydrate and is a lower risk for tube blockage compared to some other treatments." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The preferred option of this writing group is the use of Lift (or equivalent) as this will deliver the required rapid acting carbohydrate and is a lower risk for tube blockage compared to some other treatments." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-metformin-during-enteral-feeding> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of metformin during enteral feeding" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with diabetes on enteral feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-metformin-during-enteral-feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If not contraindicated, in patients already taking metformin this should be continued. Can be given as liquid preparation via the enteral feeding tube during feeding" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If not contraindicated, in patients already taking metformin this should be continued. Can be given as liquid preparation via the enteral feeding tube during feeding" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-prn-rapid-acting-insulin-for-glucose-correction> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of PRN rapid acting insulin for glucose correction" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients on enteral feeding not on VRIII with glucose >12 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-prn-rapid-acting-insulin-for-glucose-correction" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "When not on VRIII, PRN rapid acting insulin can be used to correct glucose levels >12 mmol/L however, caution should be taken when given < 4 hours before a feed break" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When not on VRIII, PRN rapid acting insulin can be used to correct glucose levels >12 mmol/L however, caution should be taken when given < 4 hours before a feed break" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-prn-rapid-acting-insulin-with-metformin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of PRN rapid acting insulin with metformin" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients on metformin with mild hyperglycaemia or uncontrolled type 2 diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-prn-rapid-acting-insulin-with-metformin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "PRN rapid acting insulin may be used alongside in accordance with local guidelines which the metformin is optimised." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "PRN rapid acting insulin may be used alongside in accordance with local guidelines which the metformin is optimised." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-same-brand-for-prn-insulin-as-quick-rapid-acting-insulin-during-feed> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of same brand for PRN insulin as quick/rapid acting insulin during feed" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients prescribed PRN insulin and quick/rapid acting insulin during feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-same-brand-for-prn-insulin-as-quick-rapid-acting-insulin-during-feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If applicable, ensure any PRN insulin prescribed is the same brand as any quick/ rapid acting insulin doses prescribed during the feed" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If applicable, ensure any PRN insulin prescribed is the same brand as any quick/ rapid acting insulin doses prescribed during the feed" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-short-term-vriii-for-insulin-naive-patients> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of short-term VRIII for insulin naive patients" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Insulin naive patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-short-term-vriii-for-insulin-naive-patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Conditional" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Insulin naive patients should be reviewed by the DIT at the earliest opportunity. Short term VRIII may be indicated in the first 24-48 hours to establish insulin requirements or optimise glucose control whilst awaiting DIT review and establishing the feeding regimen." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Insulin naive patients should be reviewed by the DIT at the earliest opportunity. Short term VRIII may be indicated in the first 24-48 hours to establish insulin requirements or optimise glucose control whilst awaiting DIT review and establishing the feeding regimen." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-subcutaneous-insulin-at-earliest-opportunity> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of subcutaneous insulin at earliest opportunity" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with hyperglycaemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-subcutaneous-insulin-at-earliest-opportunity" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Thus the use of subcutaneous insulin at the earliest opportunity to manage hyperglycaemia is desirable." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Thus the use of subcutaneous insulin at the earliest opportunity to manage hyperglycaemia is desirable." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-vriii-for-patients-with-known-type-1-diabetes-or-insulin-deficiency-when-nil-by-mouth> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of VRIII for patients with known type 1 diabetes or insulin deficiency when nil by mouth" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency who are nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-vriii-for-patients-with-known-type-1-diabetes-or-insulin-deficiency-when-nil-by-mouth" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Conditional" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If a patient with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency is nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours, a VRIII may be required if PRN rapid acting insulin is ineffective at correcting suboptimal glucose control, or the fasting state is deemed to be an increased risk for contributing to ketosis. Follow local VRIII protocols in order to avoid hypoglycaemia and achieve target glucose range 6-12 mmol/L. Continue basal insulin alongside VRIII." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If a patient with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency is nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours, a VRIII may be required if PRN rapid acting insulin is ineffective at correcting suboptimal glucose control, or the fasting state is deemed to be an increased risk for contributing to ketosis. Follow local VRIII protocols in order to avoid hypoglycaemia and achieve target glucose range 6-12 mmol/L. Continue basal insulin alongside VRIII." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-vriii-to-calculate-insulin-dose> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of VRIII to calculate insulin dose" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-vriii-to-calculate-insulin-dose" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If VRIII has been used prior to sc insulin this can be used to help calculate the dose of insulin required: consider both the total feed dose of insulin received minus 20% and the rate administered." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If VRIII has been used prior to sc insulin this can be used to help calculate the dose of insulin required: consider both the total feed dose of insulin received minus 20% and the rate administered." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-same-brand-of-prn-insulin-for-hyperglycaemia-as-prescribed-during-feed> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use same brand of PRN insulin for hyperglycaemia as prescribed during feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-same-brand-of-prn-insulin-for-hyperglycaemia-as-prescribed-during-feed" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "PRN insulin for hyperglycaemia should follow local guidance and be the same brand as any prescribed for administration during the feed, this is to allow for PRN correction doses to be added on to their feed related doses." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "PRN insulin for hyperglycaemia should follow local guidance and be the same brand as any prescribed for administration during the feed, this is to allow for PRN correction doses to be added on to their feed related doses." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/vriii-consideration-for-patients-with-type-1-diabetes-or-insulin-deficiency-who-are-nil-by-mouth> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "VRIII consideration for patients with type 1 diabetes or insulin deficiency who are nil by mouth" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency who are nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "vriii-consideration-for-patients-with-type-1-diabetes-or-insulin-deficiency-who-are-nil-by-mouth" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If a patient with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency and is nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours, a VRIII may be required if PRN rapid acting insulin is ineffective at correcting suboptimal glucose control, or the fasting state is deemed to be an increased risk for contributing to ketosis" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If a patient with known type 1 diabetes or known insulin deficiency and is nil by mouth and no enteral feed is prescribed or the feed is stopped for longer than two hours, a VRIII may be required if PRN rapid acting insulin is ineffective at correcting suboptimal glucose control, or the fasting state is deemed to be an increased risk for contributing to ketosis" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/vriii-use-in-initial-period-of-feeding> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "VRIII use in initial period of feeding" ;
    dmo:populationScope "all feed regimens" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "vriii-use-in-initial-period-of-feeding" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "VRIII may be used in the initial period of feeding to stabilise glucose and estimate insulin requirements while feeding regimen is established." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "VRIII may be used in the initial period of feeding to stabilise glucose and estimate insulin requirements while feeding regimen is established." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/when-blood-glucose-4-mmol-l-and-patient-has-recovered-give-long-acting-carbohydrate> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "When blood glucose >4 mmol/L and patient has recovered, give long-acting carbohydrate" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "when-blood-glucose-4-mmol-l-and-patient-has-recovered-give-long-acting-carbohydrate" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "When blood glucose level >4 mmol/L and the patient has recovered, give a long-acting carbohydrate. Some examples are: Restart feed; If bolus feeding, give additional bolus feed (read nutritional information and calculate amount required to give 15-20g carbohydrate); IV glucose 10% at 100ml/hr. Volume should be determined by clinical circumstances" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When blood glucose level >4 mmol/L and the patient has recovered, give a long-acting carbohydrate. Some examples are\n• Restart feed\n• If bolus feeding, give additional bolus feed (read nutritional information and calculate amount required to give 15-20g carbohydrate)\n• IV glucose 10% at 100ml/hr. Volume should be determined by clinical circumstances" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_05_enteral_feeding_guideline_april_2024> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/acute-illness> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Acute Illness" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "Patients with type 1 diabetes or significant insulin deficiency will be at increased risk of ketosis during a fasted state, acute illness or simply excess hyperglycaemia." ;
